  "text_md": "EXPLORER. It had been interrupted because of the higher priority of the LHC cost overrun discussions. The Research Board agreed to restart this procedure starting with L3+C at the next Research Board.\n\nThe next meeting of the Research Board will take place on\n\nThursday,\n\n# ENCLOSURES\n\n- [1] Minutes of the 12 th INTC meeting held on 13 May 2002 (INTC 2002-026/INTC 12)\n- [2] Minutes of the 58 th LHCC meeting held on 15-16 May 2002 (LHCC 2002-019/LHCC 58)\n- [3] Minutes of the 58 th SPSC meeting held on 21 May 2002 (SPSC 2002-022/SPSC 58)\n\n\n# REFERENCES\n\n[ 1] Minutes of the 157 th meeting of the Research Board held on 11 March 2002 (CERN/DG/RB 2001-332, M157)\n\n[ 2] Minutes of the 158 th meeting of the Research Board held on 11 April 2002 (CERN/DG/RB 2001-335, M158)\n\n[ 3] Neutron Cross Sections for the Pb Isotopes Implications for ADS and Nucleosynthesis (INTC 2001-020/P142)\n\n[ 4] Measurements of fission cross sections for the isotopes relevant to the Thorium fuel cycle (INTC 2001-025/P145)\n\n[ 5] Measurement of the neutron capture cross sections of 232 Th, 231 Pa, 234 U and 236 U; (INTC 2002-013/P154)\n\n[ 6] An Energy Upgrade of REX-Isolde to 3.1 MeV/u and Acceleration of Heavier Masses up to A=150 (INTC 2002-009/P152)\n\n[ 7] Fusion Reactions at the Coulomb Barrier with Neutron-rich Mg Isotopes (INTC 2002014/P155)\n\n[ 8] Evolution of single particle and collective properties in the neutron-rich Mg isotopes (INTC 2002-020/P159)\n\n[ 9] Summary, plan and resources of RD39 projects (LHCC 2002-015, Status Report/ RD39 1)\n\n- [10] Development of radiation hard semiconductor devices for very high luminosity colliders (LHCC 2002-003/P6)\n- [11] Status Report on the NA60 Pixel Detector Project (SPSC 2002-024/M689)\n- [12] Status Report of the HARP experiment (SPSC 2002-019/M685)\n- [13] Future plans; The DIRAC Collaboration (SPSC 2002-018/M684)\n\n\n",
